{"title":"2021 Mock AMC 8 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8bef26bffff7ebbc8c8695e0fc2ad7bb4f3c6e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2+3-4+5-6+7-8+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"261\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e700beb1d34ab2d6f887db61c5fe64c29342e3d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 6  \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"353\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 Mock AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Aaron has a rectangular yard measuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet. How many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inch by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inch rectangular bricks can he fit in his yard?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f08c63d4d90e52f7dbabb55070c8d64aad098f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 256 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 288 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"408\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 Mock AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amy, Bob, Cassie, and Darren are on a camping trip. Each of them has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for what they wear on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the camping trip. How many different arrangements of what they wear are possible on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the camping trip?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d38f38d85cd1c70393ab34c1e020265588e9015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 32 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 64 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 256 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) 500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle with positive integer side lengths has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99b9c3842e40e4102ae86b3317f26103c80cdb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. In how many ways is this possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/7752ab84e23c215afdc175282988b652ec621f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fiona leaves her house to go to the airport. She drives for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes at a constant rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour, then walks for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes at a constant rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04538d558ee93726d9441ab4aa67f0b1bdc18d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. She then goes on a train going 50 miles per hour for 12 minutes. How far has she traveled?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/959ba0506f55583fa59346fe331f0100429404b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 31.2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 32.2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 32.4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 33.8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 35.9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"471\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of this hexagon rounded to the nearest tenth?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec48d06713dd51a38d3908b8ea03b33b90c53ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 40.8 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 41.5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 41.6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 42.4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 44.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"471\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digit integer. \n</p>\n<ul><li>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square.</li></ul>\n<p>What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2add758840b316e42d3d2a6505671621c198ae62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }12\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }14\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"392\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many many zeros are at the right of the last nonzero digit of the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6caaa627cdcb0c516620d9449892c47864d67e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1020!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac5671c4efda86693458e68c81df6b199338ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }204\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }244\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }252\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }253\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }254$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd4babab25c9e82e2e8c30b21a070981213d4a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> are extended to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to make isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/094c7191712e3d340c3cff04967fb298caf61e54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units away from the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d101d36400e1d035be5c323dde0f9b85d50677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 60 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 72 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 90 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 108 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"396\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Maddie picks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that both numbers are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77c775ff741cb365eb352e540ffa8948fa79b753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58cb4555d754b24a5cf3e6c7bcebf1a039c3fcfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b01421f2b403467140cf2c6124763a2269dbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 15 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is the smallest?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a46ba91046d50e6127699a9b5cae13a5bf02ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f696facffc8d0bc4307b83f85777cd6496088835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {21}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db210b24376711e3fb53df037330f536754a3d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {5}{2} \\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb30a82304dcdd125514fb6c87d43c0cfef904f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\sqrt 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7064dea8f725f5ab8243f27b30496a7ff31e2f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {5}{3} \\sqrt 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"38\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c148c2f5ced7404b1f378309e7a21bdc135acc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\sqrt 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac {21}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac {5}{2} \\sqrt 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2 \\sqrt 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac {5}{3} \\sqrt 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"469\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degrees. What is the sum of all possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3ab960afc502d61c1c2295d7a21249d0f44c2c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~80 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~100 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~130 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~140 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Mock_AMC_8_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> have these following conditions:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488d03c7ee181b14676f499908d5721ae0d50df2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\times y = 43\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be22e3c8c1e33d3a7f55fb86c4ce880b5e4668f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + y = 37\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>What is the product of the roots of the equation?\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204751\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 412/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14333/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22097:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017204751 and revision id 245359. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}